1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:05,450
Online classes began to be popularized just a few decades ago.
仅仅几十年前，网络课程才开始普及。

2
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:16,400
They are advertised as a way for adults to finish their education and students to learn the material at their own pace—it is far more compatible with people’s busy schedules.
网络课程被宣传为一种途径，让成年人能够完成学业，让学生能够按自己的节奏学习课程内容——这种方式与人们繁忙的日程安排要契合得多。

3
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:26,210
But after being enrolled in an online course last fall semester, I came to realize online classes were merely a means to fulfil course requirements.
但去年秋季学期选修了一门网络课程之后，我逐渐意识到，网络课程只不过是满足课程要求的一种手段。

4
00:00:27,010 --> 00:00:37,930
First of all, students lack the desire to learn, and they simply complete their assignments to receive credit for a passing grade rather than genuinely engage with the course material.
首先，学生缺乏学习的愿望，他们完成作业只是为了拿到及格成绩、获得学分，而不是真正投入地学习课程内容。

5
00:00:38,730 --> 00:00:44,900
As online courses tend to have more than 100 students, most of the assignments are short and simple.
由于网络课程的学生往往超过100人，大部分作业都简短而容易。

6
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:54,150
They are not designed for students to interact with the material in depth but designed to be graded easily to accommodate such a large number of students.
这些作业的设计目的不是让学生与课程内容深入互动，而是便于评分，以适应如此庞大的学生规模。

7
00:00:54,950 --> 00:01:03,060
Perhaps the biggest disadvantage of taking an online class is the absence of face-to-face interaction between the teacher and their students.
修读网络课程最大的弊端，或许在于老师和学生之间缺少面对面的互动。

8
00:01:03,860 --> 00:01:11,120
Live sessions are infrequent and are often scheduled during the middle of the day when students have to attend other classes or work.
直播课次数很少，而且常常安排在中午前后，而这个时候学生得去上别的课或者去上班。

9
00:01:11,920 --> 00:01:17,210
The office hours of the professor may also be during inconvenient times for many students.
教授的答疑时间也可能安排在许多学生不方便的时段。

10
00:01:18,010 --> 00:01:23,110
Most interaction with the professor has to be through email, which is often impersonal.
与教授的互动大多只能借助电子邮件，而电子邮件往往缺乏人情味。

11
00:01:23,910 --> 00:01:28,380
It is nearly impossible for students to build a relationship with their professor.
学生几乎不可能与教授建立起关系。

12
00:01:29,180 --> 00:01:31,690
There is also little interaction amongst students.
学生之间的互动也很少。

13
00:01:32,490 --> 00:01:37,420
It can be harder for students to create study groups and form relationships with their peers.
对学生来说，组建学习小组、与同学建立关系可能会更难。

14
00:01:38,220 --> 00:01:44,130
Online classes also require either a computer or laptop and a reliable internet connection.
网络课程还需要一台台式电脑或笔记本电脑，以及稳定的网络连接。

15
00:01:44,930 --> 00:01:53,940
Not all students have access to these types of resources, whether it is for financial or other reasons, and some students can be put at a disadvantage.
无论是出于经济原因还是其他原因，并非所有学生都能用上这类资源，有些学生可能会处于不利地位。

16
00:01:54,740 --> 00:02:01,100
Offering online classes certainly helps students who would otherwise not be able to attend classroom sessions.
开设网络课程无疑能帮助那些原本无法到教室上课的学生。

17
00:02:01,900 --> 00:02:09,640
However, online classes fail to provide a genuine education, with an emphasis on convenience rather than critical thinking.
然而，网络课程未能提供真正的教育，注重的是便利，而不是批判性思维。

18
00:02:10,440 --> 00:02:17,730
We need restructured online classes in which students can have a learning experience that will actually provide quality education.
我们需要经过重构的网络课程，让学生能在其中获得一种学习体验，真正为他们带来优质的教育。
